Apps Not Opening

              Issue 
app /software clicks and nothing happens, or crashes immediately.
May see an error message like “App failed to start” or “This app can’t open.”

              Cause (Root cause or most likely cause)
The app didn’t install properly or is corrupted.
Windows needs updates to run the app.
User profile or temporary files are causing conflicts.

              First steps/checks
Retart computer
End the app if it’s running in rtask manager
Check Windows Updates → Install any pending updates → Restart if require
Check if the app is installed correctly:
Settings → Apps → Apps & Features → Repair or Reinstall the app.
Test the app on another user account (if possible) to see if it’s profile-related

            Escalation:
Review logs in detail
Check Event Viewer (Application + System logs)
Check crash logs and error codes for the app
>Look for red Error icons
> Match the time of the error to when the app failed to open
—- Open the error
	Double-click the error
Error name
Error code
Description


            Decide the fix
	- Permission error → fix permissions / policy
	- Missing file error → repair or reinstall app
	- System error → run SFC / DISM

2. Fix user profile issues
	Check for corrupted user profiles
	Repair or recreate the profile if needed
	Restore user data after fixing the profile
To identify a profile issue, the app tested under another user account. If it works, back up the user’s data, recreates the profile, restores the data, and confirms the application opens successfully

Repair system files
sfc /scannow
Repairs corrupted Windows system files


DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth
repairs Windows system files that SFC can’t fix, which may allow apps that failed to open due to system corruption to work properly.



Check domain / Active Directory issues
- Verify the user’s account permissions
- Check AD group membership
- Confirm the account isn’t restricted or misconfigured

Updates fix bugs in Windows or the app itself
Ensures the app has the required system files and permissions:
Install missing system patches
 Apply vendor or Microsoft hotfixes 
Ensure correct version and licensing


